 "standard_url": "https://www.education.gov.za/Portals/0/CD/National%20Curriculum%20Statements%20and%20Vocational/CAPS%20FET%20_%20MATHEMATICS%20_%20GR%2010-12%20_%20Web_1133.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Revise laws of exponents learnt in Grade 9 where x, y > 0 and m, n ∈ ℤ: xⁿ × xᵐ = xⁿ⁺ᵐ, xⁿ ÷ xᵐ = xⁿ⁻ᵐ, (xⁿ)ᵐ = xⁿᵐ, (xy)ⁿ = xⁿyⁿ; also by definition x⁰ = 1 and x⁻ⁿ = 1/xⁿ; use the laws of exponents to simplify expressions and solve easy exponential equations.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 10 exponents worksheets: laws of exponents, negative and zero exponents, simplifying and exponential equations. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "Same base: equate the exponents.",
 "key_sub": "a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>aᵐ × aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ, aᵐ ÷ aⁿ = aᵐ⁻ⁿ, (aᵐ)ⁿ = aᵐⁿ, (ab)ⁿ = aⁿbⁿ.</li><li>a⁰ = 1 and a⁻ⁿ = <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>1</span><span class='fd'>aⁿ</span></span>.</li><li>Write numbers as powers of primes to simplify: 8 = 2³, 27 = 3³.</li><li>Exponential equations: make the bases the same, then equate the exponents.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>3ˣ⁺¹ = 81</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>81 = 3⁴</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>x + 1 = 4</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x = 3</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Multiplying the bases</td><td>2³ × 2⁴ = 2⁷.</td></tr><tr><td>Negative means negative</td><td>2⁻² = ¼.</td></tr><tr><td>Different bases</td><td>Change to the same base first.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does CAPS Grade 10 say about exponents?",
   "a": "Revise the laws of exponents and use them to simplify expressions and solve simple exponential equations."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is 4⁻½?",
   "a": "That is a rational exponent (Grade 11): ½."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is (2a³)²?",
   "a": "4a⁶."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I solve 2ˣ = ⅛?",
   "a": "⅛ = 2⁻³, so x = −3."
  }
